  "description": "A node made in the same entry (state.md#a-node-made-in-the-same-entry). One entry of a files space with two ops: a `create` of a folder under the root, and a `create` of a file whose field 2 is the integer 0, the index of the first op. A node's id is the first 16 bytes of BLAKE3(entry id || varint(index)), where the entry id is the id of the signed object (encoding.md#signed-objects). What is hashed is the varint of the index, not the integer as the op encodes it: for index 1 those are the bytes 01 and 08. The file's parent is the id of the node made at index 0. Inputs are fixed bytes, not secrets.",
